Usage: w [OPTION]...

Show who is logged on and what they are doing.
On Windows, shows active terminal sessions with user, TTY, idle time.

OPTIONS:
  -a, --all      same as -b -d -u -t
  -b             omit process id from output
  -d             omit host and display fields from output
  -f, --from     print from fields
  -i             do not show idle time
  -q, --quiet    quiet output, no headings, just data
  -r             omit remote host from output
  -s             show session id instead of process id
  -t             include a header with uptime
  -u             omit user name from output
  -w             print user's tty and pid only
  -h, --heading  print heading line
  -c, --count    just print the number of logged-in users
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
